# Paper Fight

Before implementing any **gameplay** addition or change (item, monster, special, formula, targeting, spend, phase, feature), do not write the feature as soon as you hear it.

1. Read `design/paper-fight/RUBRIC.md`.
2. Overwrite `design/paper-fight/CURRENT.md` from `TEMPLATE.md`. Fill every heading.
3. Ask Nathan only the questions whose answers would change what you write (`AskQuestion`, multiple choice). Put every such question in that one batch. Stop. Do not implement in that turn. A monster pasted in the chat shorthand (`monster-shorthand.mdc`) is a Paper Fight, same as any other new card.
4. After he answers, implement the whole remaining reading in this chat. Move CURRENT into `design/paper-fight/done/`. Do not open a second question round (`finish-after-intake.mdc`). New collisions found while coding are clustered and written down; they do not stop the build.

Skip Paper Fight for: copy/art/audio only; an exact number he named on an existing rule; Ability+Flow+Notes already agree and say what happens when cards collide; he said **skip the Paper Fight** / **just ship it** / **F5 this**.

**Your notes for Cursor** (`review_note` on the board) is the spec. If that box is filled, it wins over Ability, Flow, and Notes. Do not Paper Fight to pick between them. Paper Fight only when the note itself has two readings that would change the code. Pull every gold box on every message (`content-board.mdc`). Waiting on one card’s collision questions does not pause the other gold boxes.

Quoted Ability / Call name / numbers in the note still go onto the official fields in the same turn. Wait only on the collision questions. Do not leave the old Ability on inspect while the gold box already named the replacement.

If Ability, Flow, and Notes disagree and that box is empty, Paper Fight — do not invent how this meets Hornet, Queen, or block.

For rules, this comes before same-turn guess-and-build. Feel and animation can still be built the same turn.

Worked example: `design/paper-fight/_example-copy-the-owner.md`.
